<title>CZECH REPUBLIC: Czech PM says sees 97 selloff of Leciva, Crystalex.</title>
<headline>Czech PM says sees 97 selloff of Leciva, Crystalex.</headline>
<dateline>PRAGUE 1997-03-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Czech Prime Minister Vaclav Klaus on Tuesday said he wants to increase revenue from the privatisation process in 1997, including selling off stakes in several firms once considered off limits for privatisation.</p>
<p>Klaus told a forum of business leaders that he foresaw the sale of major stakes in several key Czech firms this year, including brewery Budvar n.p., glass maker Crystalex a.s., pharmaceuticals maker Leciva a.s. and drinks maker Jan Becher-Karlovarska Becherovka a.s., maker of the herbal liqueur Becherovka.</p>
</text>
